  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rB302448-1100 Rev A \rB302448-3100 Rev A\rLocation Plan \rDesign, Access & Heritage Statement\rFlood Risk Assessment\rB302448-1000 Rev A \rB302448-3000 Rev A \r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "Unless otherwise specified in the application the materials to be used for the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted along with work of making good shall be carried out in materials to match those of the existing building.\r\rReason: To ensure that the appearance of the development respects the appearance, existing materials and built and natural features of the surrounding area.",
    "The development shall be carried out in accordance with the Flood Risk Assessment dated May 2025. The proposed surface water drainage strategy, including the installation of a soakaway, shall be implemented as set out in the Assessment. The soakaway and all associated mitigation measures shall be retained and maintained in a functional condition for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: To ensure the sustainable management of surface water on-site, minimise flood risk, avoid surface water discharge beyond the curtilage of the property, and ensure the long-term functionality of the drainage system. This is in accordance with Policy CP28 of the Core Strategy (2010), Policy DMD 61 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), Policies SI12 and SI13 of the London Plan (2021), and the National Planning Policy Framework. It also seeks to maximise opportunities for sustainable development, improve water quality, biodiversity, local amenity, and recreational value.\r"
  ]
